  "patch_packaging_note": "CS21A211H supersedes G only for the deployed Cronograma read-path repair. The browser-rendered QA bundle still used GET calls without token and required getEstudiante, which remains intentionally default-denied because its current implementation may create or update financial/structural state. H keeps that backend deny intact and rewrites only the Cronograma bundle hook to use the already-authenticated session identity plus exactly three tokenized POST text/plain reads: getGrupoInfo, getAsistenciaEstudiante and getEvaluacionesEstudiante. It also accepts grupoActivo before legacy grupo/grupos. The previously validated self URL policy (/exec or authenticated @HEAD /dev), 13 self-route aliases, Babel-safe Step3 repair, fail-closed guard and isolated QA resources remain unchanged. No PROD fallback is introduced. Local syntax validation of the replacement hook passed before this identity was promoted.",
